---
import GuideLayout from '../components/GuideLayout.astro';
import Countdown from '../components/Countdown.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import { FAQS, SYSTEM_REQUIREMENTS } from '../data/game';
import { GAME_IMAGES } from '../lib/images';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Release status', path: '/release-date/' },
];

const toc = [
  { id: 'release-date', label: 'Release date' },
  { id: 'launch-time', label: 'Launch time' },
  { id: 'price', label: 'Price status' },
  { id: 'platforms', label: 'Platforms' },
  { id: 'system-requirements', label: 'System requirements' },
  { id: 'early-access', label: 'Early Access plan' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'Release questions' },
];

const faqs = FAQS.release;
---

<GuideLayout
  seoTitle="Main Sequence: Release Date, Price & Platforms (2026)"
  description="Main Sequence launches into Steam Early Access on November 12, 2026 for Windows PC. See confirmed platforms, price status, system requirements and launch-time notes."
  eyebrow="Launch dossier"
  title="Main Sequence release date and launch status"
  intro="The Early Access date is confirmed. The price, exact unlock hour and some platform details are not. This page keeps the two categories separate."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  sourceIds={[
    'steam-news-2026-10-01',
    'steam-store',
    'steam-demo',
    'steamdb',
    'simulationdaily',
    'epic-store',
    'steam-news-2026-09-09',
    'steam-forum-controller',
  ]}
  image={GAME_IMAGES['main-sequence-freighter-departure.jpg']}
  imageAlt="A large orange and white Main Sequence freighter fires its engines while leaving a station"
  imageCaption="Main Sequence is scheduled for Steam Early Access on November 12, 2026. Official Steam screenshot."
  meta={['Update status: pre-launch', 'Windows PC', 'Early Access', 'Price not announced']}
  faq={faqs}
  pageType="WebPage"
  dataNote="Launch details can change. Check the official Steam page on release day before making a purchase or planning a stream."
>
  <section id="release-date" class="scroll-mt-28">
    <div class="panel-signal panel p-5 md:p-6">
      <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Confirmed</div>
      <p class="m-0 font-display text-4xl font-semibold uppercase leading-none text-paper md:text-5xl">
        November 12, 2026
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fog">
        Main Sequence is scheduled to launch into <strong>Steam Early
        Access</strong> for Windows PC on this date. The developer announced it
        on October 1, 2026, and the Steam store displays the same date.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      This is not a 1.0 release. The developer plans an Early Access period of
      roughly one to two years, with the final length depending on when the game
      is complete and well-rounded. The store description explicitly warns that
      the game will change during development.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-7 border border-line-soft bg-night p-4 md:p-6">
      <Countdown variant="full" class="max-w-xl" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="launch-time" class="scroll-mt-28">
    <h2>When does it unlock?</h2>
    <p>
      The publisher has not announced an exact unlock hour. SteamDB records a
      store timestamp of <strong>16:00 UTC on November 12, 2026</strong>. That is
      a useful planning reference, not an official launch promise.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the <a href="/tools/launch-timer/">launch timer</a> to see that
      timestamp converted into your local time and a table of common time zones.
      The countdown on this page uses the same estimate.
    </p>

    <div class="callout callout-warning mt-5">
      <span class="callout-title">Do not treat 16:00 UTC as official</span>
      <p class="m-0 text-sm">
        Until the publisher posts a launch-time update, 16:00 UTC is only a
        storefront listing. Steam unlock times can differ from the listed store
        date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="price" class="scroll-mt-28">
    <h2>Price: not announced</h2>
    <p>
      There is no official Main Sequence price. The October 1 release-date
      announcement said more information, including price and launch time,
      would follow. Third-party estimates are not confirmation.
    </p>
    <p>
      The developer has confirmed that the eventual 1.0 price will be adjusted
      to reflect the finished game and expanded content. That means the Early
      Access price and the final price may differ. The store page does not
      currently list a price because the game is not yet available.
    </p>

    <div class="data-table-wrap not-prose mt-5">
      <table class="data-table data-table-stack">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Item</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
            <th scope="col">Detail</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Item">Early Access price</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="unknown" label="Not announced" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="Detail">No USD, EUR or regional price has been published.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Item">Deluxe / ultimate edition</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="unknown" label="Not announced" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="Detail">No paid edition comparison exists in official material.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Item">1.0 price</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="confirmed" label="Will change" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="Detail">Expected to be adjusted based on the finished game.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Item">Demo</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="confirmed" label="Free" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="Detail">Separate free demo on Steam.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="platforms" class="scroll-mt-28">
    <h2>Platforms: Windows PC at launch</h2>
    <p>
      The official launch announcement names Steam Early Access. Steam lists
      Windows as the only supported operating system. No PlayStation, Xbox,
      Switch or macOS release has been announced, and we found no public
      statement about Steam Deck verification.
    </p>

    <div class="data-table-wrap not-prose mt-5">
      <table class="data-table data-table-stack">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Platform / service</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
            <th scope="col">What we know</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Platform / service">Steam (Windows)</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="confirmed" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="What we know">Named in the Early Access launch announcement and store page.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Platform / service">Epic Games Store</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="unknown" label="Listing exists" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="What we know">A store page exists, but the October launch announcement specifically names Steam. We are not treating Epic as the confirmed launch storefront.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Platform / service">Consoles</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="unknown" label="Not announced" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="What we know">No PS5, Xbox Series or Switch version has been announced.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Platform / service">macOS / Linux</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="unknown" label="Not announced" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="What we know">Only Windows is listed on Steam.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Platform / service">Xbox Game Pass</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="unknown" label="Not announced" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="What we know">We found no Game Pass announcement.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="cell-name" data-label="Platform / service">Controller support</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><StatusBadge status="estimated" label="Planned" /></td>
            <td class="text-sm text-mist" data-label="What we know">The developer said in 2025 that controller support was planned for Early Access launch. That is a plan, not a confirmation of every controller layout.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="system-requirements" class="scroll-mt-28">
    <h2>System requirements</h2>
    <p>
      Steam currently publishes a minimum specification only. The game is still
      in development, so treat these numbers as a baseline rather than a
      performance benchmark.
    </p>

    <div class="data-table-wrap not-prose mt-5">
      <table class="data-table data-table-stack">
        <caption class="sr-only">
          Main Sequence minimum system requirements
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Component</th>
            <th scope="col">Minimum</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            SYSTEM_REQUIREMENTS.minimum.map((item) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="whitespace-nowrap bg-deep px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-medium text-fog" data-label="Component">
                  {item.label}
                </th>
                <td class="text-paper" data-label="Minimum">{item.value}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">
      {SYSTEM_REQUIREMENTS.note} The separate Steam demo lists the same
      minimum. We have not benchmarked a retail build because it is not yet
      available to the public.
    </p>

    <h3>What the requirements mean in practice</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>8 GB RAM:</strong> sufficient for the listed minimum. If you
        often play factory games with browser tabs or voice chat open, leaving
        more memory headroom is sensible, but do not treat that as an official
        requirement.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GTX 1050 / RX 460 class:</strong> an entry-level dedicated GPU
        baseline. Integrated graphics are not listed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>5 GB storage:</strong> the listed install footprint. Patches and
        saves can add to this over time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>DirectX 12:</strong> the game calls for Windows 10 64-bit or
        newer with DX12 support.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="early-access" class="scroll-mt-28">
    <h2>What Early Access means for this game</h2>
    <p>
      The developer’s Early Access statement says the core mechanics and
      progression are fully playable at launch: ship and station design, trading
      with NPCs, fighting alien enemies, factories and automation. The current
      store estimate is around 40 hours of content.
    </p>
    <p>
      The 1.0 roadmap is not a dated checklist. The developer wants more
      building options, customization, quality-of-life features, factions, ship
      and station modules, production lines and exploration. We will not
      publish a fake roadmap with dates that have not been committed.
    </p>

    <h3>Demo save transfer</h3>
    <p>
      No official statement confirms that demo saves or builds will transfer to
      Early Access. If continuity matters, plan for a fresh start and preserve
      blueprints rather than assuming the demo state will carry over. This is
      still an unresolved question in the community.
    </p>

    <h3>Exact content at launch</h3>
    <p>
      The September 2026 playtest included later sectors, Cobalt and Graphite,
      a Trading Outpost and the Relic Destroyer, but playtest content is not a
      guarantee of launch content. The demo is a separate, limited slice. We
      label features as “demo” or “playtest” where the difference matters.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
